k. legal aid organizations;

2.3.evidence:
Article 20
(1) In order to prevent the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children, the Regional Government:
a. conducts socialization regarding the prevention of violence against women and children by optimizing the role of customary, cultural, religious institutions and community organizations;
b. provides guidelines on handling acts of violence against women and children;
c. involves community participation in recovery and reintegration; d. develops an integrated database and information system regarding acts of violence against women and children;
e. develops family empowerment programs;
f. strengthens the function of community organizations working in the field of women's empowerment and child protection; and
g. provides public facilities that are comfortable and safe for women and children.
(2) Prevention of the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be implemented by OPD whose duties and functions are in the field of:
a. social affairs;
b. health;
c. education;
d. manpower;
e. women's empowerment and child protection;
f. mental and spiritual;
g. informatics and communication; and
h. peace and order.
(3) Prevention as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be implemented by OPD in accordance with their respective fields of duty in an integrated and sustainable manner based on the Regional Action Plan.

3.10.evidence:
Article 15
Efforts to increase the role, quality and capability of women in the economic field as referred to in Article 5 paragraph (1) letter d number 4 include:
a. implementing programs, activities, training for improving the skills and expertise of women in order to realize the improvement of women's welfare;
b. facilitation of business capital strengthening for women with weak economic conditions;
c. marketing of products from businesses of women with weak economic conditions; d. training for developing women's capabilities through economic empowerment of pre-prosperous families;
e. comprehensive entrepreneurship training for women.

